<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ghiyasuddin Mahmud Shah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1533">1533</a>–<a href="/years/1538">1538</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ghiyasuddin Mahmud Shah was the last sultan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/husain-shahi-dynasty">Husain Shahi dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>, reigning from 1533 to 1538. He came to power by killing his nephew and faced the Afghan leader Sher Khan Sur, who defeated his army at Surajgarh in 1534 and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaur">Gaur</a> in 1538, despite help from Portuguese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a>. He fled and died soon afterwards.</p></div>
